  "geometry_notes": "World axes map to the source as: +Y(world, screen-up) = z-axis; +X(world, screen-right) = y-axis; +Z(world, receding toward lower-left/viewer) = x-axis. Origin sits at world (0,0,0), placed left-of-center and slightly below mid-height in the frame, matching the source where the origin is at the near-left-bottom corner of the box. Axis lines are thin black (#1a1a1a, ~1px) with small cone arrowheads, each running from origin out to ~3.6 units and extending slightly past the box face; italic labels 'x' (lower-left tip), 'y' (right tip), 'z' (top tip) placed just beyond each arrowhead. Default component magnitudes: A_x = 2.0, A_y = 3.0, A_z = 2.5 world units; the dashed box is exactly A_x × A_y × A_z (depth × width × height) with one corner at the origin, so it is close to a cube in the source. Sliders range 0–3 and the box, blue arrows, and red diagonal must all rescale together. Box edges: dashed gray (#7f7f7f), dash length ~0.12, no fill; all 12 edges drawn. Blue component arrows: dark navy #1F4E79, shaft radius ~0.035, cone head ~0.18 long, drawn from the origin along each axis with length equal to that component and lying exactly on the corresponding box edge. Red resultant: #C0392B, same shaft thickness, from origin to the opposite box corner (A_x, A_y, A_z) — the body diagonal — arrowhead landing precisely on that corner. Labels sit alongside their arrows as in the source: 'A_z = A_z k̂' rotated to run vertically just left of the z-arrow; 'A_x = A_x î' rotated to run along the x-arrow at lower-left; 'A_y = A_y ĵ' horizontal just above the y-arrow, right of center; 'A = A_x + A_y + A_z' running along the red diagonal in its middle third, all component symbols carrying overhead vector arrows. Magnitude |A| = √(A_x² + A_y² + A_z²); optional nested right triangles are the base rectangle (origin → A_x edge → xy-corner) plus the vertical rise to the far corner, drawn as thin dashed gray lines. Background white.",
